# Flood-Net station data (read-only)

Full documentation: `docs/agent-api.md`. `AGENTS.md` is the canonical agent file.

- REST API: `https://floodwarning.net/api/v1` — OpenAPI at `https://floodwarning.net/api/v1/openapi.json`.
- MCP server: `https://floodwarning.net/api/mcp` (Streamable HTTP, no auth). `.cursor/mcp.json`:
  `{ "mcpServers": { "floodnet": { "url": "https://floodwarning.net/api/mcp", "headers": { "X-FloodNet-Client": "your-name" } } } }`
- Read-only, public data only.
- Rate limits: 60 requests / 60 s per client, 20 requests / 10 s per client (burst), 240 requests / 60 s per address. On 429 wait `Retry-After`.
- Station ids are lowercase slugs (`abergowrie_br_al`); Bureau numbers also work. Search with `search_stations` / `stations_near`, then `get_station_dossier` for everything about one station, each section sourced and marked `ok`, `not recorded` or `unavailable`.
- What every gauge is saying now: `get_latest_readings` (`/api/v1/readings/latest`, by network, basin, kind or `bbox=west,south,east,north`) in one call — only telemetry ingested into Flood-Net. `format=geojson` on it and on station search answers GeoJSON for a map, points at `[lon, lat]`.
- Flood classes, crossings and flood effects are metres on the gauge (not AHD); AEP levels are modelled m AHD and indicative; the Bureau lists and the SLS give separate classes. Quote each figure's source and datum; "not recorded" is not zero.
- Flood-Net is not a flood warning service; send people to the Bureau of Meteorology for warnings.
